esai: drop the per-underrun log line

An underrun is an ordinary condition for a host-paced feed, and logging one per
frame drowns the log and costs more time than the transfer it reports on.

diff --git a/source/dsp56kEmu/esai.cpp b/source/dsp56kEmu/esai.cpp
index 5bf0bd7d..df9e955c 100644
--- a/source/dsp56kEmu/esai.cpp
+++ b/source/dsp56kEmu/esai.cpp
@@ -379,7 +379,6 @@ namespace dsp56k
 
 		if((m_writtenTX & tem) != tem)
 		{
-			LOG("ESAI transmit underrun, written is " << HEX(m_writtenTX) << ", enabled is " << HEX(tem));
 			m_sr.set(M_TUE);
 		}
 
